      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While feeling better now suggests the episode may be related to heat or dehydration, the severity of a brief \"blackout\" means it is unlikely to resolve with just electrolytes at your age. Because sudden loss of consciousness at 72 can signal an underlying cardiovascular issue that requires ruling out, delaying a medical check-up poses a real risk. I strongly recommend calling your primary care doctor or an urgent care clinic tomorrow to discuss this, which is often more accessible and affordable than an emergency room visit for a follow-up exam.",
      "source": "target",
